{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle.det3_cyclic_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle.det3_cyclic_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/OctonionCocycle.lean#L77-L87","doc":"**Fano / `PSL(2,7)` symmetry of the octonion associator (witness).** `det3` is\ninvariant under the coordinate 3-cycle `cyc ∈ GL(3, 𝔽₂)`. More generally\n`det3 (g·a) (g·b) (g·c) = det(g) · det3 a b c = det3 a b c` for **every**\n`g ∈ GL(3, 𝔽₂) ≅ PSL(2,7)` (order 168 — the Fano-plane / Klein-quartic symmetry),\nsince `det g = 1` over `𝔽₂`. This is the concrete tie between the `(ℤ/2)³`\noctonion sign structure and the genus-3 (Klein-quartic, `PSL(2,7) =` Fano) home of\nthe octonion product. Here the `cyc` generator is machine-checked; the full\n`GL(3,𝔽₂)`-invariance is determinant multiplicativity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle.cyc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle.cyc","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/OctonionCocycle.lean#L73-L75","doc":"Cyclic shift of the three `(ℤ/2)³` coordinates — a `GL(3, 𝔽₂)` element (a\n3-cycle of the coordinates, an even permutation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle.det3_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle.det3_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/OctonionCocycle.lean#L67-L71","doc":"**The deformation genuinely fires (non-associativity).** On the independent\ntriple `e₁ = (1,0,0)`, `e₂ = (0,1,0)`, `e₄ = (0,0,1)` the associator is `1 ≠ 0`:\n`(e₁e₂)e₄ = − e₁(e₂e₄)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle.det3_is_3cocycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle.det3_is_3cocycle","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/OctonionCocycle.lean#L58-L65","doc":"**The octonion associator satisfies the pentagon (3-cocycle) identity.**\nExhaustive over all `8⁴` tuples of `(ℤ/2)³`; the octonion sign rule is a genuine\ngroup 3-cocycle, pentagon-coherent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle.det3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle.det3","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/OctonionCocycle.lean#L51-L56","doc":"The `𝔽₂` determinant (trilinear alternating form) of three `(ℤ/2)³` vectors —\nthe octonion associator `φ(a,b,c)` (additive; the sign is `(-1)^φ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionCocycle.V","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/OctonionCocycle.lean#L48-L49","doc":"`(ℤ/2)³`, the octonion grading group (`8` elements index `e₀,…,e₇`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}